-- id: exp6923-v606-lifecycle-evidence-contract
-  title: V606 lifecycle-aware execution and evidence contract
-  track: infrastructure
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: claude
-  model: opus
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 100
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 150
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.606
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6923_v606_lifecycle_evidence_contract.json
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6911 blocked because it required the pre-staged `research-roadmap-next.yaml` after activation
-    had already promoted that file to `research-roadmap.yaml`. Its standalone routing audit also
-    still required Codex gpt-5.5 although the current operator directive and conductor require
-    gpt-5.6-sol. V606 has exactly 14 tasks, Exp6923 through Exp6936. This contract task is advisory;
-    no science task gates on it.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, {project_root}/CODEX.md, and {project_root}/research-program.md
-    - {project_root}/research-roadmap.yaml and, when present,
-      {project_root}/research-roadmap-next.yaml
-    - {project_root}/openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6911_v605_document_yaml_evidence_contract.json
-    - {project_root}/scripts/roadmap_schema.py, {project_root}/scripts/audit_roadmap_gates.py,
-      {project_root}/scripts/validate_prior_failures.py, and
-      {project_root}/scripts/exclusion_manifest_lint.py
-    - {project_root}/scripts/research_conductor.py only to understand activation lifecycle; do not
-      modify it
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Build a lifecycle-aware V606 document/YAML evidence contract. Audit exactly one coherent
-    roadmap state: the pre-staged next file before activation or the active file afterward. Align
-    the standalone model-routing audit with the current Codex gpt-5.6-sol directive. Require exact
-    document/YAML parity, valid gates, declared gate fields, prior-failure retirement mechanics,
-    prompt structure, model policy, two infrastructure slots, one SOTA-ingestion slot, independent
-    science roots, and an ungated capstone. Do not alter either roadmap while auditing it.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require the design document, exactly one lifecycle-resolved V606 execution
-       file, current validators, and the exclusion manifest. If resolution is ambiguous or inputs
-       are missing, write complete_blocked_v606_lifecycle_evidence_contract with
-       gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-REPORT-6923 and focused tests before implementation. Cover pre-staged, activated,
-       missing, mismatched, and ambiguous roadmap states plus current Codex model routing.
-    2. Resolve the roadmap lifecycle without merging task lists. Require milestone `2026.09.606`,
-       exactly 14 tasks, Exp6923-Exp6936 in order, and the exact documented deliverables.
-    3. Parse the document and YAML independently. Compare ID, title, order, deliverable, gate,
-       milestone, model-bearing task, infrastructure-slot, SOTA-slot, and ungated-tail rows.
-    4. Require CONTEXT, EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST, TASK, CONCRETE STEPS, one Run command, and the
-       exact mandated final sentence in every prompt.
-    5. Prove every structured gate names an upstream task in this roadmap and a field declared in
-       that upstream task's own REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS. Reject aliases.
-    6. Validate all prior-failure entries, including non-empty addressed_by text and
-       `retire_if_same_verdict=true`, against the exclusion manifest.
-    7. Update the standalone routing audit and its tests so Codex formulaic tasks require
-       gpt-5.6-sol. Do not weaken agent/model cross-vendor checks.
-    8. Prove Exp6923, Exp6924, Exp6925, Exp6926, Exp6929, Exp6932, Exp6935, and Exp6936 are ungated;
-       prove no science task gates on Exp6923 or Exp6925.
-    9. Emit one row per check. Set `v606_execution_contract_ready_score=1` only when all hard checks
-       pass. This score cannot promote a science claim.
-    10. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, YAML/schema validation, prior-failure validation,
-        gate audit, exclusion lint, artifact-convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, docs
-        audit, and root-clutter checks.
-    11. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one principle per required field and
-        `v606_execution_contract_ready_score`; preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-        (deterministic_lifecycle_manifest_and_evidence_audit_no_llm); duration_s;
-        source_artifact_hashes; rows; lifecycle_resolution_rows; document_task_rows;
-        yaml_task_rows; document_yaml_parity_rows; gate_contract_rows; required_field_rows;
-        prior_failure_contract_rows; model_contract_rows; prompt_ending_rows;
-        infrastructure_slot_rows; sota_ingestion_slot_rows; independent_root_rows;
-        ungated_tail_rows; routing_audit_update_rows; task_count; experiment_range; random_seed;
-        reproducibility_checksum; v606_execution_contract_ready_score; gate_check_summary with
-        failed check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-        verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked |
-        disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal and prefixed complete_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6923_v606_lifecycle_evidence_contract.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
