-- id: exp6926-span-first-relation-fixture
-  title: Exact span-first relation fixture
-  track: acquisition
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 240
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.606
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6926_span_first_relation_fixture.json
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6915 qualified only 8 model relation events, all Gemma-31B graph-coloring. Free-form relation
-    text lost exact anchors and direction for the other required models and four relation families.
-    V606 changes the proposal interface: the model must first copy two verbatim source spans, then
-    name their directed relation. Exact code, not a model judge, maps copied bytes to offsets and
-    checks semantics.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6912_alias_safe_relation_corpus_reducer.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6915_sota_model_relation_event_bank.json
-    - Exp6913 and Exp6914 scripts, tests, and artifacts
-    - relation corpus producers and exact tuple/ASP/isomorphism checkers
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md and
-      {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Build a deterministic, source-grounded relation fixture and plain-text protocol. Each proposal
-    contains exactly two verbatim span lines and one directed relation line. Freeze UTF-8 byte
-    offsets, five relation families, positive/negative/unknown cases, paraphrases, isomorphic
-    renamings, and exact ASP consequences. Do not use JSON schema, constrained decoding, repair
-    reprompts, finite answer IDs, or a model judge.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require readable clean source rows, exact relation/ASP/isomorphism checkers,
-       and stable UTF-8 byte handling. On failure, write complete_blocked_span_first_relation_fixture
-       with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-VERIFY-6926 and tests first. Cover repeated spans, Unicode, overlaps, reverse
-       direction, absent spans, ambiguous duplicates, negation, unknown relations, malformed lines,
-       paraphrases, and entity-renamed isomorphs.
-    2. Define the three-line plain-text protocol and deterministic parser. Resolve spans against the
-       immutable source bytes before interpreting relation labels.
-    3. Generate balanced fixture rows for graph coloring, scheduling, allocation, precedence, and
-       exclusion. Include positive, negative, and unknown labels in every family.
-    4. Freeze calibration and held-out fixture partitions by seed and content hash. Do not expose
-       held-out expected outputs in live prompts.
-    5. Recompute byte offsets, direction, canonical tuple, ASP effect, and isomorphic invariance in
-       a fresh process. Retain every invalid row and exact rejection reason.
-    6. Set `span_relation_fixture_ready_score=1` only when all family/label cells exist, all hashes
-       replay, ambiguity is explicit, and exact checkers agree.
-    7. Emit one per-example row and one per mutation/replay row. No aggregate-only claim is allowed.
-    8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, deterministic replay, adversarial verification,
-       artifact-convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one principle per required field and
-       `span_relation_fixture_ready_score`; preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-       (deterministic_cpu_span_first_fixture_no_llm); duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows;
-       fixture_rows; protocol_rows; utf8_offset_rows; ambiguity_rows; relation_family_rows;
-       label_balance_rows; asp_effect_rows; isomorphism_rows; mutation_rows; partition_rows;
-       heldout_hash_manifest; parser_rejection_rows; random_seed; reproducibility_checksum;
-       span_relation_fixture_ready_score; gate_check_summary with failed check, expected value, and
-       observed value for any blocked verdict; verifier_is_oracle (true); verdict_class
-       (circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal and
-       prefixed complete_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6926_span_first_relation_fixture.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
-  prior_failures:
-    - experiment_id: exp6915-sota-model-relation-event-bank
-      verdict: complete_disqualified_qualified_relation_event_bank_thresholds_not_met
-      addressed_by: 'This attempt replaces free-form relation extraction with exact verbatim span copying before direction assignment and validates byte offsets before semantics.'
-      retire_if_same_verdict: true
